# PHASE 1: local.properties points at the customer's Android SDK install.
# Created by the customer's Android Studio on first project open, or generated by:
#   echo "sdk.dir=C:\\\\Users\\\\<USER>\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Android\\\\Sdk" > local.properties
# Replace the path with the real Android SDK location on the build machine.
# This file is git-ignored in the production repo.

# V2.3 / V18 — Firebase Cloud Messaging. The values below are injected into
# BuildConfig at build time and used by com.restaurant.staff.fcm.RestaurantFirebaseApp
# to construct FirebaseOptions. To get them:
#   1. Create a project in Firebase Console (https://console.firebase.google.com)
#   2. Add an Android app with package name com.restaurant.staff
#   3. Copy the three values from "Project Settings" -> "Your apps"
# Leaving them blank means push notifications are disabled and the in-app feed
# still works via REST polling. The server side sees status=SKIPPED for FCM.
# restaurant.fcm.projectId=
# restaurant.fcm.appId=
# restaurant.fcm.apiKey=
# restaurant.fcm.messagingSenderId=